eded to understand here and in  other cities that you have to do  business a different way  [Music]  the role of the monitor is to come in  and to oversee police reform such as how  the police department used force our  trained its officers our disciplined its  officers I remember vividly the  monitoring effort was extremely  difficult  they were extremely antagonistic towards  me and the monitoring team the process  wasn't easy I saw the police department  coming kicking and screaming because we  had done business the way we had done  business for so many years  the default stance that most police  agencies have is big me little you we  tell you what we are going to do to make  your community safer and we're going to  tell you how we're going to do it  I think problem-oriented policing is  just the opposite it is problems that  are organically driven up from the  community and that you strategically  work to improve that situation with  input from community members you know he  looks at  [Music]  our citizens complain Authority gives us  the opportunity to do our own  investigation citizens feel is if they  have issues they have a place to go an  independent body that's not part of the  city will take their complaint and  investigate it each contact with the  citizen whether of the traffic staff  whether it was a field interrogation  stop you had to fill out the contact car  name age race why you were making this  stop and the cry was more paperwork more  work for the police but in the end that  work through that time period helped  assist us to get us to where we are now  complaints started going down so those  cars did help change the mindset of this  interaction with the city so we still do  them absolutely  I'm a member of the quality of life  enhancement team unit this is a lot  different than running a beat because  I'm able to focus on my target area for  my entire shift I'm not getting  dispatched on to different radio runs we  interact with these kids for 